# AI Agent Model Lanes

This project uses LiteLLM as the client-facing gateway for local and provider
model lanes. Cursor agents should use the lane names and role boundaries below
instead of talking directly to individual vLLM runtimes.

Gateway:

```text
http://litellm.hom.lab/v1
```

Profile contract:

```text
/Users/joshc/develop/dotfile-vnext/.cursor/ai-agent-profiles.json
```

## Rules

- Use `litellm.hom.lab` as the gateway surface when a custom OpenAI-compatible
  base URL is available.
- Do not point Cursor directly at `vllm-runtime`, localhost, or one-off node
  ports for normal project work.
- Preserve the user-approved model lane set. Do not collapse work to
  `ornith-35b@k3s02-vllm~coder-primary` just because it is the first runtime path.
- Client `model_name` syntax: `<model-slug>@<host-slug>~<friendly-lane>` (see
  `roles/k3s_litellm_gateway/defaults/main/model_client_ids.yml`). Most entries are
  **FRIENDLY ALIAS** routes; `complexity-router@litellm~smart-router` is a
  **MODEL GROUP** (complexity auto-router).
- Treat model catalog entries with `pending_research` or `provisional_example`
  status as not selected for download or pinning.
- Include trace metadata in tool/client wrappers when available:
  `agent_role`, `model_lane`, `routing_policy`, `context_class`.

